# EXAMPLE knowledge-skill document (generic). Derived from the operator-tuned
# original with profile-specific anchors replaced by <PLACEHOLDERS>. Copy to
# $TREEBEARD_BASE/shared/toolbox/data/skills/<name>.txt and fill placeholders
# from your own career profile before use.
SKILL: fit_scorer (career_hunter package)
CONSUMER: governed Han turn. INPUT: career_profile.txt + candidates.json
from career_search. OUTPUT: per-job scores, evidence-based.

PURPOSE
Score each candidate job against THIS operator, not an abstract ideal
applicant. Every score must cite which profile facts drove it. A score
without cited evidence is invalid.

DIMENSIONS -- score each 0-5, integer, with one line of evidence:
  transferable_experience   does the operator's actual prior work (EXAMPLE:
                            PM/PO/program/BA/writing) credibly
                            map onto this role's real duties
  qualification_match       would a screener reading the resume see the
                            stated requirements credibly met (stretch is
                            fine; fiction disqualifies the score, not the operator)
  compensation_probability  likelihood the role clears the bands in the
                            profile; use posted comp when present; UNKNOWN
                            comp scores 3, never 0 (flag, don't discard)
  work_location_fit         remote=5; <PRIMARY_CITY>/<COMMUTABLE_AREA> commutable hybrid=4;
                            other hybrid=1; relocation required=0
  interview_likelihood      honest odds of a first-round (if the profile
                            marks a career change, apply the usual
                            screener discount); index pages and
                            600-applicant reposts score low
  career_change_friction    inverse: 5 = uses the operator as-is, 0 = requires
                            retraining or a credential the operator lacks
  application_time_roi      value of the outcome x odds, divided by the
                            effort the application demands (portals with
                            essays score low unless the fit is exceptional)

HARD RULES
- previously_pursued companies: score normally but state the prior
  pursuit; a DIFFERENT role at the same company is fair game.
- company_flag entries (strong negative preference): cap total at MAYBE
  tier unless evidence is exceptional; say why if you break the cap.
- stale_evidence or source_tier 7-8: treat claims skeptically; an index
  page or aggregator repost is NOT a live application target -- score
  interview_likelihood accordingly and say so.
- below-floor compensation: score honestly, FLAG in the evidence line,
  never silently drop. If the profile declares an urgency rule, apply it
  (EXAMPLE: credible fast-to-employment lateral roles are not
  hard-rejected on pay).
- Never invent job details not present in the candidate record; if the
  record is too thin to score a dimension, score it 2 and mark THIN.

OUTPUT per job: {"url", "total": 0-35, "scores": {<dim>: int}, 
"evidence": {<dim>: "one line"}, "thin": bool}
